{"resourceIdentifier":"4047","resourceName":"CLIMATE SUSTAINABILITY THROUGH HORTICULTURE PROJECT IN INDIA","description":"This is an Afforestation/Reforestation Project on degraded and fallow land and lies within the boundaries of India. The purpose of this grouped project is to promote the restoration of degraded and fallow land and improve the living conditions of farmers by planting horticulture and commercial species (indigenous species preferred). This is a grouped project.\r\n\r\nThe first project activity instance under the program is located in the state of Maharashtra, district Nandurbar in India. TATA Communications Limited (TCL) has implemented the VPA01 from 01-April-2022 with the coordination of implementing entity Collectives for Integrated Livelihood Initiatives (CINI). The area covered in this VPA is up to 303 hectare with an average land holding of approximately 0.40 hectare or one acre per farmer.\r\nThe villages under the project area predominantly have an agrarian economy. The conditions of lands covered under the project are either barren & fallow land with seasonal crops grown. The plantation under the project activity will lead to the sequestration of CO2 at a faster pace. \r\n\r\nThe technology used for the tree plantation is simple as it just involves procurement of saplings from designated nurseries and planting various empty and barren locations of the districts. The first VPA is estimated to sequester average 5,645 tCO2e annually over 20 years.","location":{"latitude":21.819400,"longitude":74.235000},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-06-13","endExclusive":"2023-07-14","endInclusive":"2023-07-13"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4047"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Tata Communications Limited"},{"type":"string","value":"National Capital Territory of Delhi, India"